{{Term/Store|Lightning||Series, BotW, TotK, HWL, HWDE, CoH}} is a recurring mechanic in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|Oh dear, oh dear... {{Color BotW|Red|Lightning}} strikes this stable so often, I get nervous whenever it rains even a little.|Cima|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Yikes! Rain! Ooh, I sure hope we don't get any {{Color TotK|Red|lightning}}... Ugh. I'm going somewhere dry.|Trott|TotK}}</ref><ref name="Log">{{Cite|{{Color HWDE|Red|Lightning}} is striking the temples! {{Color HWDE|Blue|Hyrulean Forces}} are losing health!|Battle Log|HWDE}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|You got some {{Color CoH|Yellow|lightning arrows}}!|Game Screen|CoH}}</ref>{{Name Ref|LANS}}

==Overview==
==={{LA|-}}===
Lightning can be seen during the opening of {{LA}}. As [[Link]] sails through a [[Thunderstorm]], his boat is struck by Lightning and destroyed.

==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Stub|BotW}}
Lightning occurs during [[Thunderstorm]]s, striking sporadically. Any metallic [[Weapon]]s, [[Shield]]s, or [[Bow]]s, including those equipped by [[Link]] or an [[Enemy]], will spark during Thunderstorms and eventually attract a Lightning strike on their position (which will deal extreme damage to Link if he does not either remove the offending equipment before the strike happens or equips the [[Thunder Helm]] to neutralize the strike). Other metallic [[Object]]s will also attract Lightning, requiring Link to keep his distance to avoid being hit by a Lightning strike.

==={{TotK|-}}===
Lightning occurs during [[Thunderstorm]]s, striking sporadically and functioning in the same way as it did in {{BotW}}. Lightning also appears in the cloud cluster around the [[Thunderhead Isles]].

[[Thunder Gleeok|Thunder]] and [[King Gleeok]]s shoot beams of Lightning at [[Link]] that electrocute him if he is not wearing [[Armor]] with [[Shock Resistance]] or the [[Lightning Proof]] [[Added Effect]].<ref>{{Cite|Been to the {{Color TotK|Red|Coliseum Ruins}} before? They're opposite Outskirt Stable, inside the rocky mountain, but I hear they're occupied by a {{Color TotK|Red|big monster}}. Some kind of three-headed beast that breathes {{Color TotK|Red|lightning}} at you if you get close. Sounds like a bad time to me, even if I had lightning-proof gear. I think I'll stick to research, thanks.|Savelle|TotK}}</ref> These Lightning beams will still harm Link with or without either of these Added Effects. When Thunder or King Gleeoks are badly damaged, they cause Lightning to strike the ground, creating [[Updraft]]s at their impact site.

==Other Appearances==
==={{HWL|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
In the "[[Watchers of the Triforce]]" [[Scenario]], [[Phantom Ganon]] makes use of Lightning to attack the [[Hyrulean Forces]].<ref name="Log"/> The Lightning can be protected against through the power of the [[Sage]]s.<ref>{{Cite|If we don't stop Phantom Ganon, then the lightning will never cease.|Cia|HWDE}}<br/>{{Cite|There is another way. The power of the sages. It can protect us!|King Daphnes|HWDE}}</ref> When a [[Warrior]] is struck by Lightning, they lose one quarter of a [[Heart]].
{{Noncanon|End}}

